# Deny-all allowlist. Order matters: the last matching pattern wins, so the
# blanket deny comes first, the allow rules after it, and the test denials
# last so they override the allow rules above them.
*

# Allowed files, at the repo root only. A name with no slash matches in every
# directory, so each one carries a leading slash; a nested ignore file or a
# nested README can then not reopen the deny-all.
!/.gitignore
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE

# Assets and everything under them.
!assets/
!assets/**

# Every directory is re-included, because a negation cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded. Files inside stay denied by `*`
# unless an allow rule below names them.
!*/

# Crate manifests, build scripts and sources.
!crates/**/Cargo.toml
!crates/**/build.rs
!crates/**/*.rs

# The pictures the README shows (made-up mail only).
!screenshots/
!screenshots/*.png

# Tests are never tracked. These come after the allow rules on purpose.
*.tests.rs
**/tests/

# The font files and their license texts live outside Git while the build
# setting `font_source` is "outside" (build-support/build-settings.toml). This
# comes after every allow rule, so the assets rule above cannot reopen it.
# Remove this line only in the same change that sets `font_source` to "tracked".
assets/fonts/
